        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3dd1a72a-2dac-5e61-bbec-ebe307da9ed8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pink Gin, Pink Plymouth, Gimlet, Plymouth gin, Angostura bitters, Rose's Lime Juice Cordial\n- Places: England\n- Publications: The Savoy Cocktail Book\n- Topics: Cocktail ingredients, cocktail proportions, cocktail history\n\nFacts:\n- In the mid-19th century, Pink Gin, also called Pink Plymouth, became fashionable in England.\n- Pink Gin consists of Plymouth gin and a dash of Angostura bitters.\n- Angostura bitters is a dark red bitters that gives Pink Gin a pinkish color.\n- In 1930, The Savoy Cocktail Book specified a Gimlet proportion of one half Plymouth Gin and one half Rose's Lime Juice Cordial.",
